	(text "Cell and reverse protection" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 25.4 45.72 0) (effects (font (size 2 2)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "67119178-e4f8-5b66-8e6d-2603205db02e"))
	(text "Q1 conducts through its body diode at insertion,\nthen Vgs = -VBAT turns it fully on.\nReversed cell: Vgs ~ 0, Q1 stays off.\nOnly C3 + C7 (1.1 uF) stay on VBAT: the 100 uF bulk's\nIR spec (50 MOhm.uF -> 0.5 MOhm) could leak ~6 uA always-on." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 25.4 111.76 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "08dc1ff2-1934-59c4-81b5-2296695c358c"))
	(text "LCD supply switch" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 99.06 45.72 0) (effects (font (size 2 2)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "15f61730-05d2-5f0d-b962-194a2f09f3a8"))
	(text "LCD boost" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 149.86 45.72 0) (effects (font (size 2 2)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "ea33676b-47eb-5dde-ae5f-3fb4fc065cb6"))
	(text "U5 TPS22916C (TI SLVSDO5F); U3 TPS61099 (TI SLVSD88M).\nLid shut: U5 off (ISD 10 nA typ, 100 nA max) removes the boost's\n0.5-1.6 uA shutdown current and C2's leakage from the cell.\nU5 slew alone (~2-3 mV/us at 3 V) would pull 220-350 mA into C2 + C4;\nR4 limits it to ~6.6 mA (tau ~52 ms nominal).\nR5/C8 hold the boost off until C2 is charged: EN reaches 1.2 V after\n~0.24 s (LCD_PWR_EN = 3.0 V) to ~0.37 s (2.2 V)." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 25.4 132.08 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "693399f9-0d35-5345-a618-4ea0ae4af39b"))
	(text "VOUT = VREF x (1 + R1/R2) = 1.00 V x (1 + 402k/200k) = 3.01 V\n(PWM; in PFM VREF is 1.03 V typ -> ~3.10 V)\nR2 <= 200k keeps divider current >= 100x FB leakage (50 nA max).\nL = 1 uH (datasheet: 1 uH for VOUT <= 3.0 V).\nCOUT >= 20 uF nominal -> 2 x 10 uF." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 134.62 111.76 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "b35fdc24-1260-5842-8636-94a408583bcf"))
	(label "VBAT_RAW" (at 38.1 58.42 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "b6f005d3-8a84-5e00-87e5-edfbd8850874"))
